  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "A new roof in Utah typically costs between $9,500 and $18,000 for a standard single-family home with architectural asphalt shingles. On average, homeowners with a 2,000-square-foot roof spend around $11,000 to $15,000.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "between $9,500 and $18,000"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Final pricing depends heavily on your chosen material, roof size, and local climate requirements.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          3,
          4
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Average Cost by Material"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Roofers measure and price jobs by the \"square,\" which equals 100 square feet of roof surface. According to the 360 Roofing Utah Cost Guide , installed prices across the state break down as follows:",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "360 Roofing Utah Cost Guide",
            "link": "https://360roofingutah.com/guides/roof-replacement-cost-utah"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Average Cost by Home Size"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Because roof pitch and overhangs add surface area, your roof is usually larger than your home's interior footprint. Estimates from Bigfoot Roofing Utah show typical shingle replacement ranges by home size:",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Small homes (under 1,500 sq. ft.). Expect to pay between $7,500 and $10,500."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Average homes (1,500 \u2013 2,500 sq. ft.). Costs generally fall between $10,000 and $14,500."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Larger homes (2,500 \u2013 3,500 sq. ft.). Replacements usually range from $13,500 to $19,000.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Factors That Drive Up Utah Quotes"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Roof pitch and complexity. Steep slopes, multi-story access, and multiple valleys or dormers increase labor costs by 15% to 30%.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Snow and ice protection. Utah building codes and mountain climates require heavy-duty ice and water shields along the eaves to prevent winter ice dams.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tear-off and decking repairs. Removing more than one layer of old shingles adds labor and disposal fees. If contractors find rotted plywood underneath, replacing damaged sheets typically adds $60 to $125 per sheet.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              4,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Local permits and disposal. Dumpster fees generally run $350 to $450, while municipal building permits cost $50 to $200 depending on your city or county.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "(Note: If your roof has recent hail or wind damage, homeowners insurance often covers the replacement minus your deductible.)",
        "reference_indexes": [
          4
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To give you a more tailored estimate, tell me a bit more about your project:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What is the approximate square footage of your home?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Which material are you leaning toward (standard shingles, impact-resistant shingles, or metal)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What city or region of Utah are you located in (e.g., Wasatch Front, mountain towns, or Southern Utah)?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
